Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: a bsta_cap for a radio in its em_config waits for the next topology

Every Topology Response that carries the Backhaul STA Radio Capabilities TLV submits a
bsta_cap request for that radio (em_configuration's topology handler), whatever the radio's
state, and build_candidates queues it on the radio's em. bsta_cap only runs on a configured
radio (is_em_ready_for_orch_exec), so a request for a radio still in its em_config (M2 sent)
waited in the pending queue, its query never sent, until its time limit; the radio's
configuration then ran over its own budget and the controller renewed the agent. With a pod
whose second radio reports the TLV from its first Topology Response, that repeated every
minute for 7 minutes after a physical pod's boot (12 October). The same class as 0207 for
unassociated-STA queries: a bsta_cap whose radio cannot run it is refused at submit, with no
statistics registered and the radio's owner untouched; the next topology sync (about 15 s)
asks again, and it runs once the radio is configured. gen/tests/bsta-cap-admission-test.py
reproduces the block with --expect-blocked on the unpatched source.

Platform-independent.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/src/orch/em_orch.cpp b/src/orch/em_orch.cpp
index 9311b027..7cf1ac52 100644
--- a/src/orch/em_orch.cpp
+++ b/src/orch/em_orch.cpp
@@ -153,7 +153,13 @@ bool em_orch_t::submit_command(em_cmd_t *pcmd)
         // if there are no candidates, complete the command
         destroy_command(pcmd);
     } else {
-        if (pcmd->m_type == em_cmd_type_unassoc_sta_query) {
+        // A Backhaul STA Capability request comes with every Topology Response that carries
+        // the Backhaul STA Radio Capabilities TLV, whatever its radio's state. Queued behind
+        // that radio's em_config it can never run (bsta_cap runs on a configured radio), so it
+        // waited out its time limit and held the radio's configuration until a renew, over and
+        // over. Refused like an unready candidate query; the next topology sync asks
+        // again, once the radio is configured.
+        if (pcmd->m_type == em_cmd_type_unassoc_sta_query || pcmd->m_type == em_cmd_type_bsta_cap) {
             bool ready = eligible_for_active(pcmd);
             for (unsigned int index = 0; ready && index < queue_count(pcmd->m_em_candidates); ++index) {
                 auto *radio = static_cast<em_t *>(queue_peek(pcmd->m_em_candidates, index));
